    "body": "EICMA 2026 • MTPeak Stole Some of the Spotlight at EICMA 2026 With Insane Power and Retro Looks on Three Wheels\nHonda Avancier Debuts With Six Seats, New Logo, and New Hybrid Powertrain\n13 photos\nPhoto: Honda\nThe all-new 2027 Honda Avancier arrives as a three-row, six-seat hybrid SUV. It comes with the next-generation hybrid powertrain and the newly styled brand logo, sits on a new platform, and is the first of 15 models of its kind that Honda plans to roll out globally by 2030.\nPositioned above the CR-V in Honda’s lineup, the Avancier is the first hybrid model to wear Honda’s redesigned, minimalist \"H\" logo , which matches its entire design. The Avancier features sharp horizontal lines, smooth body surfaces, flush-fitting door handles, and a dramatically sloping roofline.\nThe model comes with a split-headlight front-end layout with slim upper LED daytime running lights and lower main beams, flanking a bold grille, paired with a full-width LED light bar and tall vertical accents, featuring straight lines and 90-degree angles out back, where a thin tailgate spoiler with a concealed rear wiper shows up.\nHonda is obviously pushing for a visually uncluttered and sleek silhouette. Higher-spec models like the top-of-the-line RS ride on 20-inch alloy wheels and get blacked-out mirror caps and rear privacy glass for more drama.\nPhoto: Honda Unlike typical seven-seat models in the segment, the new Avancier launches strictly as a six-seater. The second row hosts two seats separated by a fold-down center console with cupholders for a limousine-like space and comfort.\nDeveloped under the \"Grand Journey\" concept, the cabin can be specced with the optional Relaxation seats and upscale materials, along with a panoramic sunroof, which confirm its rivalry with the Hyundai Santa Fe, Kia Sorento, and Mazda CX-80.\nHonda installed its 15-inch central touchscreen on board, along with a digital instrument cluster and an optional head-up display. The model sports a 12-speaker BOSE Premium Sound System, compatible with Dolby Atmos for an immersive 3D sound experience.\nA voice recognition function for controlling features such as the air conditioning, Remote In-Cabin View, and Remote Surround View are also on the menu. Honda will add post-purchase features with over-the-air (OTA) updates.\nPhoto: Honda Honda keeps powertrain details under wraps, but the all-new Avancier, built on a newly developed lightweight architecture, replaces the previous e:HEV system with a new, downsized, higher-efficiency hybrid system.\nThe system is expected to integrate a 2.0-liter petrol engine with two electric motors, operating in the automaker’s first electric all-wheel-drive layout, the DualPower eAWD. The electric motors, one mounted out front and another driving the rear wheels, will work independently to put down power and improve off-the-line acceleration as well as stability.\nThe SUV is also equipped with the Motion Management System (MMS), an integrated vehicle-dynamics control technology that coordinates steering, braking force, and hybrid driving force to stabilize the SUV and sharpen its cornering.\nThe Avancier will also get the Honda S+ Shift, borrowed from the Prelude and Civic e:HEV RS, to simulate gear shifts and deliver a more engaging feel behind the wheel. The space was designed specifically to reduce physical strain and fatigue even during long-distance travel.\nPhoto: Honda The Honda Avancier will roll off the production line of the brand’s Prachinburi plant in Prachinburi Province, Thailand, and will launch first in Thailand, Japan and China before arriving in Australia and New Zealand in April 2027. The automaker currently has no plans to sell the Avancier in North America, where the larger Pilot and Passport fill the lineup.\nPricing has yet to be released, but Australian media claims the model is expected to start at around 60,000 Australian dollars, which translates to roughly $40,058 U.S. This would position it as a rival for the Hyundai Santa Fe, Kia Sorrento, and Toyota Highlander .\nHonda has big hybrid plans The all-new Avancier is the first of 15 next-generation hybrid models that Honda will launch by the end of the fiscal year ending March 31, 2030. The plan follows a pivotal strategic moment when the automaker canceled almost its entire electric 0 lineup, including the 0 Saloon, 0 SUV , and Acura RSX, to reallocate funds to hybrids. Only the 0 Alpha has survived .\nThe Japanese automaker is expected to launch the next-generation Honda CR-V in 2027. Built on the same new midsize architecture as the all-new Avancier, the redesigned CR-V will arrive in North America as a hybrid-only crossover with the same 2.0-liter two-motor setup and DualPower eAWD.\nIn the meantime, the Civic and Accord, already previewed by the Honda Hybrid Sedan Prototype, are expected to debut around early 2028 and carry over the same hybrid system as the Avancier and the CR-V. The Acura Hybrid SUV Prototype previewed a future Acura RDX , set to arrive in either late 2027 or early 2028.\nHonda has already announced a major wave of U.S. investments totaling more than $3.8 billion across its plants in Ohio, Alabama, and Georgia. The move follows the rising demand for hybrids and the tariffs imposed by the Trump administration on imported cars. The investments will help the Japanese automaker increase its production capacity to 1.3 million vehicles per year.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more stories from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\n2027 honda avancier Honda Honda hybrid honda australia Honda 2.0\nDownload: 2027 Honda Avancier (PDF)\nAbout the author: Elena Luchian\nElena started off as a sports reporter and five years later switched to automotive. How does that happen? Lots of writing, testdrives, traveling, off-road driving courses, track driving courses, defensive driving courses and diplomas. The diplomas might be \"useless\", but the knowledge she gained is priceless. Full profile\nUP NEXT Burn It at the Stake! A Designer Set His Sights on a VW Transporter Van and Tried To Make It a Coupe",
